  "title": "Kourovka problem 20.39 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let F be a non-abelian finitely generated free group, 1 ̸= w ∈ F , and n ⩾ 1.\nIs the group ⟨F, t | tn = w⟩ linear of degree 2 over a field of characteristic 0 if w is\nnot a proper power in F ?\n    This question is motivated by the following well-known question: is it true that\nthe free Q-group F Q is linear over a field? (See 13.39(b).)        A. Jaikin-Zapirain",
    "sha256": "370e4e357b6e36f8b927bae8f2922af1cce50f650190ff71228e71dd1c19cd18",
